+# Check PlaceBlock arguments with t
+
+Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker and moves the PlaceBlock
+handler's argument checks onto it. Remotes added later can use t the same way.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `pesde.toml`: adds `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }`, installed from Wally
+  through pesde like the other packages. 3.1.1 is the latest version on the Wally index. It
+  installs to `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau`: the hand-written `typeof` and NaN checks
+  become one t checker, `t.tuple(t.string, isPosition)`. `isPosition` is `t.Vector3` plus a NaN
+  check, because `t.Vector3` checks only the type and accepts a NaN position.
+- `README.md`: adds t to the packages table.
+
+All the checks the handler made before still run, in the same order:
+
+| Check | Before | Now |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof` | `t.string` |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof` | `t.Vector3` |
+| Position is not NaN | `position ~= position` | NaN check inside `isPosition` |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | unchanged |
+| Rate limit (`MIN_INTERVAL`) | | unchanged |
+| Character has a `HumanoidRootPart` | | unchanged |
+| Cell is not below Y = 0 and not already filled | | unchanged |
+| Cell is within `MAX_REACH` | | unchanged |
+
+The game-state checks stay in the handler because they depend on the player and the world, not
+on the argument types. t's checkers don't narrow Luau types, so the handler casts the two
+arguments after the check passes.
+
+## Before testing
+
+1. **Run `pesde install`** from the repo root, with `rojo serve` stopped (Rojo 7.7.x can crash
+   while pesde rewrites `roblox_packages`). Until you do, `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t` doesn't
+   exist and the script errors on load.
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** to this branch. The install writes the t entry to it, and
+   this PR doesn't include that change because nothing was installed when it was written.
+3. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp can see t:
+   `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`.
+4. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo plugin in your dev place.
+
+## Testing
+
+Run without the package installed: `selene` and `stylua --check` pass on the changed script.
+`luau-lsp analyze` reports one error, `Unknown require: game/ReplicatedStorage/Packages/t`, which
+is expected until t is installed and the sourcemap regenerated. Not yet run: the install and a
+playtest. Please check:
+
+- `luau-lsp analyze` (command in the README) passes after steps 1 to 3 above.
+- In a playtest, a valid placement still places a block.
+- From the client (the command bar switched to the client during a playtest), firing
+  `PlaceBlock` with a non-string
+  name, a non-Vector3 position, `Vector3.new(0 / 0, 0, 0)`, or an unknown block name places
+  nothing and logs no error.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
